    "Communication between agents is facilitated through the Agent2Agent (A2A) protocol.",
    "The A2A protocol provides a standardized interaction layer that is agnostic to the underlying frameworks used by the agents.",
    "The A2A protocol enhances security by leveraging established web mechanisms such as TLS and OpenIDConnect.",
    "The A2A protocol addresses unique challenges posed by autonomous agent operations.",
    "Reliance on traditional web security models presents limitations for autonomous agents.",
    "There is a necessity to rethink security frameworks tailored specifically for LLM-based AI agents.",
    "LLM-based AI agents utilize a combination of self-sovereign identities, verifiable credentials, and standardized protocols to autonomously retrieve information, perform calculations, and ensure secure collaboration across organizational boundaries."
] 

